13 — MULTI-RECIPIENT DELIVERY FLOW

Implement the following delivery lifecycle.

Global route

1. Business creates the route.
2. Business enters multiple recipients.
3. Business defines packages.
4. Business chooses a vehicle.
5. Business schedules the route or requests immediate dispatch.
6. Driver is assigned.
7. Driver arrives at pickup point.
8. Business confirms parcel handover.
9. Driver starts route.
10. Route tracking becomes active.
11. Driver navigates to the next recipient.

Individual delivery lifecycle

Each recipient has an independent delivery status.

Statuses:

* Pending
* Scheduled
* Driver assigned
* Driver approaching pickup
* At pickup
* Package collected
* In transit
* Approaching recipient
* Arrived
* Delivered
* Failed
* Rescheduled
* Cancelled

When the driver begins moving toward Recipient A:

* Recipient A receives a notification.
* Recipient A receives access to their tracking page.
* Recipient A sees the driver location.
* Recipient A sees an estimated arrival time.

When Recipient A’s delivery is confirmed:

* Recipient A’s delivery is completed.
* The recipient’s tracking link reflects completion.
* The driver proceeds to Recipient B.
* Recipient B becomes the active delivery.
* Recipient B receives the appropriate notification.
* Recipient B gains access to the live tracking experience.

Continue this process automatically for each recipient.

The merchant sees the complete route and all delivery statuses.

Recipients see only their own delivery.

